Zero-initialise the VL buffers that HDF5's dimension-scale code reads attributes into.

H5DSiterate_scales (and the five other functions in hl/src/H5DS.c that read the
DIMENSION_LIST or REFERENCE_LIST attribute) allocate one `hvl_t` per dimension of the
dataset with malloc and fill them with H5Aread. An attribute that holds fewer entries
than the dataset has dimensions leaves the rest of the buffer unwritten, and the code
then reads buf[dim].len and dereferences buf[dim].p from that uninitialised memory
(found by fuzzing a corrupt UGRID netCDF file through nc_inq_var -> get_attached_info
-> H5DSiterate_scales; ASan's malloc fill shows as 0xbebebebebebebebe). calloc makes an
unwritten entry empty (len 0, p NULL), which the existing `len > 0` test already skips,
and gives H5Treclaim on the failure path nothing to free from it.

This is a local fix for the instrumented fuzz build, not a backport: it has not been
reported or fixed upstream as far as the maintainers know (HDF5 1.14.6). Same size, same
behaviour on every valid file.

--- a/hl/src/H5DS.c
+++ b/hl/src/H5DS.c
@@ -302,7 +302,7 @@
             goto out;
 
         /* allocate and initialize the VL */
-        buf = (hvl_t *)malloc((size_t)rank * sizeof(hvl_t));
+        buf = (hvl_t *)calloc((size_t)rank, sizeof(hvl_t));
         if (buf == NULL)
             goto out;
 
@@ -358,7 +358,7 @@
             goto out;
 
         /* allocate and initialize the VL */
-        buf = (hvl_t *)malloc((size_t)rank * sizeof(hvl_t));
+        buf = (hvl_t *)calloc((size_t)rank, sizeof(hvl_t));
         if (buf == NULL)
             goto out;
 
